Create the file `apps/flashcards/app/src/data/themes/solfege.json` with exactly 21 flashcards covering 7 notes × 3 durations.

Top-level structure:
```json
{
  "id": "solfege",
  "name": "Solfège",
  "cards": [ ... ]
}
```

Card structure for each of the 21 cards:
```json
{
  "id": "<note-fr>-<duration-en>",
  "label": "<fr> / <EN>",
  "front": {
    "renderEngineId": "score",
    "data": { "clef": "treble", "notes": [{ "note": "<VexKey>", "duration": "<dur>" }] }
  },
  "back": {
    "renderEngineId": "score-audio",
    "data": { "clef": "treble", "notes": [{ "note": "<VexKey>", "duration": "<dur>" }] }
  }
}
```

Note FR → VexFlow mapping: do→C4, ré→D4, mi→E4, fa→F4, sol→G4, la→A4, si→B4
Duration EN → VexFlow: whole→"w", half→"h", quarter→"q"
Card ID pattern: `<note-fr>-<duration-en>` — ré is encoded as `re` in IDs (no accent)
Label format: `do / C`, `ré / D`, `mi / E`, `fa / F`, `sol / G`, `la / A`, `si / B`

Card ordering: iterate notes in order [do, ré, mi, fa, sol, la, si], then durations in order [whole, half, quarter] for each note. So 21 cards total: do-whole, do-half, do-quarter, re-whole, re-half, re-quarter, mi-whole, ..., si-quarter.

Both front and back `data` objects are identical (same clef, same notes) — only `renderEngineId` differs: `score` for front, `score-audio` for back.

Validate: the resulting JSON must be valid, contain exactly 21 cards, and all cards must have the `label` field.

Update `apps/flashcards/app/src/types/index.ts` to add an optional `label` field to the `Card` interface.

Current `Card` interface:
```typescript
interface Card {
  id: string;
  front: CardSide;
  back: CardSide;
}
```

Update to:
```typescript
interface Card {
  id: string;
  label?: string;
  front: CardSide;
  back: CardSide;
}
```

This allows solfege.json cards to carry a top-level `label` field (e.g. `"do / C"`) while keeping all existing themes working without changes (the field is optional).

No other changes to this file. Do not change any exports.
